secure-exec: load a precompiled XKB keymap instead of forking xkbcomp

third_party/xserver/ is large and not tracked in VCS (it is fetched/reconstructed
out of band), so the secure-exec X-server source patches live as patch files here.
This one makes the wasm X server usable WITHOUT a working keyboard-config toolchain:
wasi has no fork/exec, so Xvfb cannot run `xkbcomp` to compile a keymap at runtime,
its keyboard device never activates, and every KeyPress/XTEST event is dropped.

Fix: install a host-precompiled US keymap at /xkb/default.xkm (scripts/prepare-xkb.sh
+ --vm-tree) and load it directly in XkbCompileKeymap(). It is read through fmemopen
because VFS-backed files do not support per-access fseek/fread streaming under wasi
(the same limitation freetype hit) and XkmReadFile fseeks to each section offset.

After applying, rebuild + REMEMBER to re-apply wasm-opt --fpcast-emu:
    scripts/link-xvfb.sh && wasm-opt --fpcast-emu -O0 Xvfb.wasm -o Xvfb.wasm

Apply with: patch -p1 < patches/xserver-keymap-no-xkbcomp.patch   (from third_party/xserver)

--- a/xkb/ddxLoad.c
+++ b/xkb/ddxLoad.c
@@ XkbCompileKeymap @@
     /* These are the components we really really need */
     need = XkmSymbolsMask | XkmCompatMapMask | XkmTypesMask |
         XkmKeyNamesMask | XkmVirtualModsMask;

+    /* secure-exec: wasi has no fork/exec, so the server cannot run xkbcomp to compile a keymap (and the
+     * rules->components lookup also needs the xkb config tree). Prefer a keymap precompiled on the host
+     * and installed at /xkb/default.xkm: XkmReadFile is pure file I/O and works under wasi. This gives
+     * the server a real keymap so the keyboard device activates and KeyPress/XTEST + XLookupString work
+     * (e.g. typing into the st terminal emulator). Falls through to the normal xkbcomp path if absent. */
+    {
+        FILE *pf = fopen("/xkb/default.xkm", "rb");
+        if (pf) {
+            /* secure-exec: VFS-backed files don't support per-access fseek/fread streaming under wasi
+             * (same limitation freetype hit), and XkmReadFile fseeks to each section offset. Slurp the
+             * whole file and hand XkmReadFile a real seekable in-memory stream via fmemopen. */
+            long sz;
+            char *blob = NULL;
+            if (fseek(pf, 0, SEEK_END) == 0 && (sz = ftell(pf)) > 0 &&
+                fseek(pf, 0, SEEK_SET) == 0 && (blob = malloc((size_t) sz)) != NULL &&
+                fread(blob, 1, (size_t) sz, pf) == (size_t) sz) {
+                fclose(pf);
+                FILE *mf = fmemopen(blob, (size_t) sz, "rb");
+                if (mf) {
+                    XkbDescPtr pre = NULL;
+                    unsigned missing = XkmReadFile(mf, need, XkmAllIndicesMask, &pre);
+                    fclose(mf);
+                    if (pre != NULL && ((need & ~missing) == need)) {
+                        free(blob);
+                        ErrorF("secure-exec: loaded precompiled keymap /xkb/default.xkm\n");
+                        return pre;
+                    }
+                    if (pre != NULL)
+                        XkbFreeKeyboard(pre, 0, TRUE);
+                    ErrorF("secure-exec: /xkb/default.xkm unusable (missing=0x%x)\n", missing);
+                }
+                free(blob);
+            } else {
+                free(blob);
+                fclose(pf);
+                ErrorF("secure-exec: failed to slurp /xkb/default.xkm\n");
+            }
+        }
+    }
+
     xkb = XkbCompileKeymapForDevice(dev, rmlvo, need);

     return KeymapOrDefaults(dev, xkb);
 }
